WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.589
It's going to be a big year for spooky new
supernatural series, whether we're talking

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:07.040
about haunted houses or magical adventures.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.420
From high fantasy to horror and everything
in between, these are the TV shows we're looking

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.240
forward to in 2020.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.600
Netflix has so much content that you'll basically
never run out of shows to power through, especially

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.020
when it comes to genre shows.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.860
The real problem is finding the good ones.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.070
Here's a hot tip for this year's marathon
viewing: if you're a fan of supernatural drama,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:27.960
then absolutely check out Spectros.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:33.120
It's a new Brazilian series from writer/producer
Douglas Petrie, and if his name sounds familiar,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.770
you might just recognize it from two truly
iconic spooky shows, Buffy the Vampire Slayer

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.000
and American Horror Story: Coven, on which
he served as a writer and producer.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.260
The eight-episode first season is set to introduce
viewers to the Liberdade district of Sao Paulo,

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.580
Brazil, the home to a large and vibrant Japanese
population.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.360
Because of this blending of cultures, the
story which follows five teenagers as they

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.120
encounter the supernatural will be an intriguing
mix of Brazilian folklore and Japanese ghost

00:00:59.120 --> 00:00:59.700
stories.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.620
Season 1 of Spectros is set to debut on Netflix
on February 20.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:08.960
Dispatches From Elsewhere, the new AMC series
created by Jason Segel, looks like it has

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.680
the potential to break out of the narrow confines
of genre into something truly unexpected.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.020
Trailers for the series frame it as an interesting
hybrid of conspiracy thriller, psychedelic

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.000
adventure, and uplifting journey of self-discovery.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.880
There are plenty of questions begging for
answers as the characters search for a mysterious

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:29.229
woman named Clara and argue over whether or
not what they're doing is a real quest or

00:01:29.229 --> 00:01:30.400
just an elaborate hoax.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.159
With that in mind, we really don't know how
much fantasy will actually be involved in

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.080
this series, but we can't wait to find out.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:41.280
With an ensemble cast that includes Academy
Award winner Sally Field, André 3000 of Outkast

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.000
fame, and others, Dispatches from Elsewhere
arrives March 1.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.000
Unless you've been hiding out in a bunker
for the past decade or just woke up from a

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.840
coma, you probably know a thing or two about
The Walking Dead.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.920
It began as a comic book series and then expanded
to television in 2010, where it quickly became

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.700
one of the biggest things in the history of
cable TV.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.600
Since then, the flagship series in the franchise
has continued its run on AMC, and a spinoff

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.679
series titled Fear the Walking Dead has enjoyed
its own successful run.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:12.060
Now, in 2020, it's time for yet another expansion.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.820
In addition to a promised series of films
starring original Walking Dead hero Rick Grimes,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.880
the Walking Dead universe is adding a third
series to its ranks with The Walking Dead:

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.600
World Beyond.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:25.620
This new series will take us into the story
of the first generation of young people who've

00:02:25.629 --> 00:02:27.579
actually grown up with the apocalypse.

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:30.799
They've come of age in a world of privilege,
behind walls that protected them from the

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:31.620
walkers beyond.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.470
Now it's time for them to venture out into
the hellish landscape for the first time,

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.659
and we can't wait to see what that looks like.

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:39.409
World Beyond premieres April 12.

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:45.090
Though it reached a climax of sorts with Avengers:
Endgame in 2019, the Marvel Cinematic Universe

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.760
isn't slowing down any time soon.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:51.360
We'll be seeing new characters and old favorites
from Marvel for years to come, and a lot of

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.779
that is going to be happening on the small
screen.

00:02:53.779 --> 00:02:58.150
That includes plenty of new shows including
The Falcon and the Winter Soldier and WandaVision

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.200
arriving on Disney+ in the coming months,
but even that's not all.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:05.760
We'll also be seeing new interpretations of Marvel heroes over on Hulu, including Helstrom.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:11.560
Helstrom is based on the Marvel Comics characters Daimon and Satana Helstrom, who in their original forms

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:18.660
are presented as the literal children of Satan. In the new Hulu series, Daimon and Ana are cast as the children of a

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:25.080
horrific serial killer, who attempt to make amends for their father's wrongs by hunting down the worst that humanity has to offer.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:31.400
Much like Doctor Strange before it, we can
expect Helstrom to dig into some of the more

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.560
occult-heavy corners of the Marvel Universe,
and we'll find out exactly how it does that

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.320
when the series lands on Hulu at some point
in 2020.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:42.360
Penny Dreadful launched in 2014 as a new take
on the pulpy, sensationalized fiction from

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:43.970
which it derived its title.

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:48.150
Over the course of three seasons, viewers
met familiar faces ranging from the vampire-hunting

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:52.979
Abraham Van Helsing to Victor Frankenstein
and his infamous monster or monsters, as the

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:57.089
case may be and saw them re-interpreted in
exciting new ways that made for an addictive

00:03:57.089 --> 00:03:58.089
horror series.

00:03:58.089 --> 00:04:01.700
Now, in 2020, the next chapter in the Penny
Dreadful story begins.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:06.269
While the original series took place in the
1800s and had a very European feel, Penny

00:04:06.269 --> 00:04:10.489
Dreadful: City of Angels will move its location
to exactly where the title suggests.

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:14.329
The new series is set in Los Angeles during
the Golden Age of Hollywood, and because of

00:04:14.329 --> 00:04:19.910
its California roots it will also pull heavily
from Mexican folklore for its subject matter.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.650
Viewers can look forward to plenty of horrific
new delights, including demons walking the

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.450
Earth and the Mexican deity Santa Muerte.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:30.080
Starring Natalie Dormer of Game of Thrones
and The Hunger Games fame, Daniel Zovatto,

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.720
Nathan Lane, and more, Penny Dreadful: City
of Angels arrives on April 26.

